{"tool_name":"glint","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"glint","home":"https://github.com/cozygene/glint/releases","summary":"User-friendly toolset for the analysis of high-throughput DNA-methylation array data.","addition_date":"2018-06-05T12:49:08Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:38:25.603543Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:glint","credit":[{"email":"ehalperin@cs.ucla.edu","name":"Eran Halperin","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"elior.rahmani@gmail.com","name":"Elior Rahmani","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://glint-epigenetics.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Whole genome methylation analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3206"}]}],"name":"GLINT","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"d.gabrielaitis","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btx059","metadata":{"abstract":"GLINT is a user-friendly command-line toolset for fast analysis of genome-wide DNA methylation data generated using the Illumina human methylation arrays. GLINT, which does not require any programming proficiency, allows an easy execution of Epigenome-Wide Association Study analysis pipeline under different models while accounting for known confounders in methylation data. Availability and Implementation: GLINT is a command-line software, freely available at https://github.com/cozygene/glint/releases. It requires Python 2.7 and several freely available Python packages. Further information and documentation as well as a quick start tutorial are available at http://glint-epigenetics.readthedocs.io.","authors":[{"name":"Halperin E."},{"name":"Rahmani E."},{"name":"Schweiger R."},{"name":"Shenhav L."},{"name":"Weissbrod O."},{"name":"Yedidim R."},{"name":"Zaitlen N."}],"citationCount":41,"date":"2017-06-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioin